00:02:52.589 --> 00:02:54.130
and turning it into
something useful.

00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:58.772
The next step falls to
the business analyst,

00:02:58.772 --> 00:03:00.230
where they actually
have to develop

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:02.010
some kind of an
understanding of the data.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:02.510
Right?

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:06.950
This may be things like just
early analytical queries,

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:09.230
something that gives
them a sense of what does

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:10.710
this data really look like.

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:13.126
We're not going to have the
data engineer figure that out.

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:14.540
It's really on
them to transform.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:16.340
Then, it falls into
the business analysts

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.650
to understand what's
inside that data set.

00:03:21.691 --> 00:03:23.690
Well then, we're going
to get to model building.

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:25.356
So the first step for
the data scientist

00:03:25.356 --> 00:03:27.520
