00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:36.980
other than this is the
Cloud Storage Bucket,

00:20:36.980 --> 00:20:39.750
where I actually dumped the
MovieLens 20 million rating

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:41.070
data set into.

00:20:41.070 --> 00:20:43.710
So you can see these are
just the raw CSV files.

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:47.420
They're not terribly exciting
at this part of it, quite yet,

00:20:47.420 --> 00:20:51.876
but now we can actually
start Dataprep flow.

00:20:51.876 --> 00:20:53.250
So what I did,
inside of Dataprep

00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:56.190
is I started a new flow, and
I imported those data sets.

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:58.910
I said, here's where my data
lives inside of Google Cloud

00:20:58.910 --> 00:21:02.160
Storage, and now I actually
want to take some action on it.

00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:04.520
So the first one was
the Movies data set,

00:21:04.520 --> 00:21:08.007
if you remember, and we
executed this cleanup phase.

00:21:08.007 --> 00:21:09.590
So I want to switch
to my cleanup tab.

00:21:09.590 --> 00:21:11.095
I'm going to show you.

00:21:11.095 --> 00:21:13.315
So inside of Dataprep,
as I mentioned earlier,

00:21:13.315 --> 00:21:15.190
you can see across the
top that it's actually

00:21:15.190 --> 00:21:18.370
sampling all of these
columns and showing me

00:21:18.370 --> 00:21:20.977
the distribution of data in
them, which is actually pretty

00:21:20.977 --> 00:21:22.810
handy, again, as you're
trying to figure out

00:21:22.810 --> 00:21:25.610
what is in these data sets.

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:27.640
And so what you're seeing
right now on screen

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:29.200
is actually the
